{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The main modeling decision is becoming narrower: epithelial descendants will inherit shape once the root epithelial term is axiomatized, but non-epithelial `squamous`/`cuboidal` classes need direct treatment. I’m checking those specific cases now so I don’t over-assert shape on variable-form classes like endothelial or thyroid follicular cells."}}
